.TH NTAG424-SDM 1 "2026-06-27" "libnci 1.0.0-alpha.1" "libnci manual"
.SH NAME
ntag424-sdm \- verify a Secure Unique NFC (SUN) message from an NTAG 424 DNA
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ntag424-sdm
.RI [ options ]
.IR URL | mirror-data
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ntag424-sdm
parses and cryptographically verifies the SDM / SUN data produced by an
NTAG 424 DNA tap: the encrypted PICCData (UID + read counter), the optional
encrypted file data, and the truncated SDMMAC. Given the relevant AES keys it
decrypts the PICCData to recover the real UID and monotonic counter and reports
whether the SDMMAC is VALID. It is an offline verifier \(em no NFC hardware is
required \(em suitable for the server side of a tap-to-verify flow.
.SH OPTIONS
See
.B ntag424-sdm --help
for the full set of key and offset options, which mirror the SDM file
configuration written by
.BR ntag424-provision (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the SUN message verified, non-zero on a parse failure or an invalid MAC.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nfc-read-ndef (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Part of the libnci NFC stack.
